# 1️⃣ DATA MODEL (with mock data)

### Core Form Schema (driven by backend)

```json
{
  "formId": "user_onboarding",
  "fields": [
    {
      "id": "email",
      "type": "text",
      "label": "Email",
      "required": true,
      "validators": ["required", "email", "unique"]
    },
    {
      "id": "country",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "Country",
      "api": "/api/countries"
    },
    {
      "id": "state",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "State",
      "dependsOn": "country",
      "api": "/api/states?country={value}"
    },
    {
      "id": "city",
      "type": "select",
      "dependsOn": "state",
      "api": "/api/cities?state={value}"
    }
  ]
}
```

---

### User Input State (normalized)

```js
{
  values: {
    email: "jeni@gmail.com",
    country: "IN",
    state: "KA",
    city: "Bangalore"
  },

  errors: {
    email: "Already exists",
    state: null
  },

  touched: {
    email: true,
    state: false
  },

  loading: {
    stateOptions: true
  }
}
```

👉 Normalized = scalable, no deep nesting

